---
// Engineering Journal landing — full custom page bypassing Starlight chrome.
// Inner pages (Projects/Writing/Stack/About) remain Starlight-managed.
import '../styles/custom.css';

const today = new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-GB', {
	year: 'numeric',
	month: 'long',
	day: 'numeric',
});
const volume = `Vol. III · No. ${new Date().getFullYear() - 2022}`;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<meta name="description" content="Ahmad Asmar — Staff DevOps / Platform Lead. AWS, EKS, GitOps, Kubernetes, Kyverno, Crossplane, Istio Ambient. Open-source maintainer of a 3,767-download Terraform Registry module and a 158★ Claude Code skills marketplace." />
		<title>Ahmad Asmar — Staff DevOps / Platform Lead</title>
		<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
		<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
		<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
		<link
			rel="stylesheet"
			href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght,SOFT@9..144,300..900,0..100&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap"
		/>
		<meta property="og:title" content="Ahmad Asmar — Staff DevOps / Platform Lead" />
		<meta property="og:description" content="3 years building Zencity's AWS-native platform. 20 EKS clusters, 4 regions, 25+ microservices. Open-source maintainer." />
		<meta property="og:url" content="https://ahmedasmar.github.io" />
		<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
		<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
	</head>
	<body class="ej-body">
		<main class="ej-landing">
			<!-- Masthead -->
			<header class="ej-masthead">
				<div class="colophon">
					<span class="ej-vol">{volume}</span>
					<span>{today}</span>
				</div>
				<nav class="colophon">
					<a href="/projects/terraform-runner-module/">Projects</a>
					<a href="https://medium.com/@ahmed.asmar" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Published</a>
					<a href="/writing/scale-to-zero-runners/">Writing</a>
					<a href="/stack/">Stack</a>
					<a href="/about/">About</a>
				</nav>
			</header>

			<!-- Hero -->
			<section class="ej-hero">
				<p class="ej-eyebrow">Ahmad Asmar · Portfolio</p>
				<h1 class="ej-title">A platform,<br /><em>by hand.</em></h1>
				<p class="ej-role">
					<span>Staff DevOps</span><span class="dot"></span>
					<span>Platform Lead</span><span class="dot"></span>
					<span>CKA</span><span class="dot"></span>
					<span>Open to opportunities · GMT+3</span>
				</p>
			</section>

			<!-- Section: TL;DR -->
			<div class="ej-rule" role="presentation">
				<span class="label"><span class="ord">§ I.</span> &nbsp;Field notes</span>
				<span class="line"></span>
				<span class="crosshair">+&nbsp;&nbsp;+&nbsp;&nbsp;+</span>
			</div>

			<section class="ej-tldr">
				<p>
					<strong>Six+ years</strong> scaling cloud-native infrastructure across AWS, GCP,
					and Azure. The last three of those as senior platform owner for a SaaS-scale
					AWS-native platform (Zencity, via ASAL Technologies): grown from a hybrid
					Azure+AWS estate into a <strong>20-account, 4-region, 20-EKS-cluster</strong>
					system serving 25+ microservices and 20+ government customers across the US and
					UK. Sole DevOps engineer for the first <strong>18 months</strong>, then primary
					IC for the next 18. The migration close-out shipped with zero customer-visible
					downtime; the last fleet-wide EKS upgrade landed in <strong>two working days</strong>.
				</p>
				<p>
					Before Zencity: <strong>Freightos</strong> (2021–2023) — GCP, Kubernetes,
					GitOps with ArgoCD, monitoring; <strong>PDF Solutions</strong> (2020–2021) —
					cloud infrastructure-as-code; plus two years of IT-support roots at
					<strong>Partners for Sustainable Development</strong> and
					<strong>Palestine Telecommunications</strong>. Open-source maintainer of a
					Terraform module powering self-service GitLab runner fleets
					(<strong>3,767 downloads</strong> on the Terraform Registry, 2 years of
					maintenance) and a Claude Code skills marketplace for DevOps workflows
					(<strong>158 ★ · 32 forks</strong>).
				</p>
			</section>

			<div class="ej-ledger" aria-label="Headline metrics">
				<div class="cell">
					<div class="figure">3,767</div>
					<div class="caption">Terraform Registry downloads</div>
					<div class="note">ahmedasmar/gitlab-docker-autoscaler-runner — v0.6.8, GPL-3.0</div>
				</div>
				<div class="cell">
					<div class="figure">158 ★</div>
					<div class="caption">devops-claude-skills</div>
